{
  "name": "Mini Refinery Horizon: Full-on (Level 3a)",
  "notes": [
    "Three crudes (A, B, C) on two CDUs plus a Diesel HDS (90 kt capacity). Crudes B and C can run on CDU-1 or CDU-2; crude A only on CDU-1.",
    "Calibrated by Moeve (as Intermediate): higher sulphur in crudes A, B and C, CDU-1 capacity 180 kt, CDU-2 at 5.5 EUR/t and HDS capacity 90 kt, so that a high HDS severity pays off economically.",
    "Diesel HDS between the pool and blending; it treats the whole pool. Outlet sulphur and yield follow Moeve's Kero-HDS relation (Appendix B5), see refinery.hds_outlet. Cost 10 + 8 z^2.2 EUR/t of feed. Cetane unchanged; the yield loss is gas with no value.",
    "hds_severity levels: null = bypass (unit off, no cost), then z = 0, 0.5, 1. Feed must not exceed the HDS capacity when the unit runs.",
    "All crude and product prices, yields and qualities are taken from Moeve's fictional 'Refinery Horizon' case.",
    "Netbacks for light products, atmospheric residue and hydrocracker feed are added for this reduced case (Moeve's full case models those units explicitly).",
    "Standard Diesel takes whatever is left in the pool: standard_share = 1 - premium_share - hydrocracker_share.",
    "encoding: every decision on qubits (pool split and import in intervals). encoding_mixed_integer: only the operating mode on qubits; pool split and import are continuous (see refinery.complete_plan)."
  ],
